		{"id":"rq2","type":"text","text":"RQ2 Strategies & support\nstudent + instructor · pedagogic · tools","x":-660,"y":714,"width":260,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"rq1","type":"text","text":"RQ1 Challenges\ninterpret · create · refine · evaluate","x":-660,"y":132,"width":260,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"rq3","type":"text","text":"RQ3 Socio-technical conditions\ntools · course · domains · feedback","x":-1160,"y":1252,"width":260,"height":108,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ph3","type":"text","text":"PH3 — Want checks and explanations, not auto-drawn homework [finding]\nAcross tools and AI, people ask for validation and help understanding — not a machine that draws the assignment.","x":1520,"y":896,"width":380,"height":166,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ph1","type":"text","text":"PH1 — Turning a written problem into the first diagram [finding]\nThis is the hard, under-taught step. Learning symbol names is easier than making that first model.","x":1520,"y":180,"width":380,"height":150,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ph2","type":"text","text":"PH2 — No auto-check, so the teacher is the “right/wrong” signal [finding]\nUnlike code, a model does not compile. Students mostly learn they are wrong when a teacher tells them.","x":1520,"y":575,"width":380,"height":157,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"oq5","type":"text","text":"Open: student evidence for abstraction claim?","x":2260,"y":949,"width":280,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"oq1","type":"text","text":"Open: dedicated refine/rework challenge?","x":2260,"y":570,"width":280,"height":60,"color":"1"},
